    <ImplementationPlan>
      <T-001>
        <Title>Rename repositories and make preference reads write-free</Title>
        <DependsOn />
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Use descriptive identity and credential repository names in matching files, constructors, callers, and compile-time interface checks. Split SQLite credentials into its own repository and route all queries/writes through the transaction-context executor.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Return a valid kg default plus a presence flag when preferences are absent, without saving. Expose presence through GetPreferencesResult and adapt CreateSet to consume the default without creating preferences.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Test absent/present preference reads and credential operations in transactions using temporary databases; retain existing domain and persistence coverage.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification>
          <Command>go test ./internal/domain/... ./internal/infra/persistence/sqlite ./internal/app/...</Command>
        </Verification>
      </T-001>
      <T-002>
        <Title>Implement real Dropbox authorization and atomic questionnaire completion</Title>
        <DependsOn>T-001</DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Add an application identity-linking port with authorization URL and code-exchange capability. Implement Dropbox authorization-code/S256 PKCE and offline token exchange without redirect_uri, using an injected browser launcher and HTTP client.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Configure the public Dropbox app key via DROPBOX_APP_KEY. Request minimal account_info.read scope, use the verified token response account ID, enforce token/expiry validity, and report generic sanitized HTTP errors.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Encrypt access and refresh tokens with AES-GCM and a lazily created private local key file; no key or application rows are written on an all-skipped flow. Support cancellation, bounded HTTP requests, and browser-open fallback.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Add CompleteQuestionnaire accepting optional unit and optional authorized identity/credentials. Validate through domain constructors; return without a transaction when both are omitted, and otherwise persist selected answers atomically. Wire the handler and real linker into bootstrap.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Test PKCE payloads, exchange failures, encrypted round trips/tamper rejection, no-write skipping, and transaction rollback without contacting a live account.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification>
          <Command>go test ./internal/infra/dropbox ./internal/app/command ./cmd/cli</Command>
        </Verification>
      </T-002>
      <T-003>
        <Title>Replace secondary screens with the full-screen startup and reset questionnaire</Title>
        <DependsOn>T-002</DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Open unit setup only when GetPreferences reports no row; preserve ordinary record-model test construction. Add r from records to reopen a fresh questionnaire without deleting settings or browsing state.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Use a focused text input with numeric choices 1. kg / 2. lb and 1. Dropbox, explicit skip hints, and an additional code-entry step for real authorization. Stage answers and write only at completion; Escape cancels, and global quit remains available.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Keep browser authorization and code exchange asynchronous and cancellation-aware, discard stale messages after reset/cancel, and retain a usable questionnaire on invalid input or save errors. Apply an explicitly saved weight unit to visible sets after successful persistence.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Render a full-screen active-color frame with main-view border/padding and an in-bounds native input cursor; handle resizing, compact/tiny output, and long status/authorization text.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Remove Preferences and Sync source/test files, their routing/App bindings, and p/s help entries; document r as reset setup. Preserve ge/gs and dialog/help input isolation.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Add TUI layout/navigation tests and temporary-database startup/reset/partial/skip/link/cancel/error integration coverage. Review intended help golden updates, then validate without snapshot regeneration.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification>
          <Command>go test ./internal/infra/tui/... ./cmd/cli</Command>
        </Verification>
      </T-003>
      <T-004>
        <Title>Update GRACE projections and validate the integrated change</Title>
        <DependsOn>T-003</DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Retire M-TUI-PREFERENCES-SYNC and its verification anchor, route M-TUI-QUESTIONNAIRE, M-APP-QUESTIONNAIRE, and M-INFRA-DROPBOX-AUTH, and update affected graph/verification entries and indexes centrally.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Synchronize source semantic contracts/maps/blocks for governed edits, preserve unrelated projection entries and workspace edits, and run full tests, vet, formatting checks, selected target, and final assertions.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Archive this completed work after passing fresh final evidence under the user instruction to archive every GRACE work; do not modify approved assertions, tasks, or scopes in place.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification>
          <Command>go test ./...</Command>
          <Command>go vet ./...</Command>
        </Verification>
      </T-004>
